# Figures and math in the design

- Figures: a fenced `mermaid` block. No ASCII-art diagrams. A directory tree or a code signature in a code block is not a diagram.
- Math: inline `$...$`, display `$$...$$`. Do not use `\(` or `\[`. Do not put `$` inside a code block.
- A new formula does not reuse a symbol defined nearby with another meaning ($N$ for the points and $W$ for the plot width in pixels stay what they are wherever they appear).
- An ordered list (the frame stages, the steps of a resize, the levels of a pyramid build) is written in one place. A section that adds to it names the steps it follows and points back.
- Code in the design is C# pseudo-code that follows `.cursor/rules/csharp.mdc` naming, so it can be copied into an implementation without renaming.
- Japanese prose is plain form (常体). Do not run the `natural-japanese` rewriting on code or formulas.

````text
# BAD — a box-and-arrow drawing of the frame stages in a plain code block
# GOOD
```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Input --> Viewport --> Lod[LOD selection] --> Upload --> Draw --> Present
```
````
